<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπεράω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go over</i> or <i>across,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελάγη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἐπ᾽ οἶδμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					395
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πόλιν</span>
			<i>pass through</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1264
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Ἑλλάδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					117
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εἰς Ἰταλίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					485
				</span></i>
			; of Time, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὸν βίον</span>
			<i>pass through</i> life, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				11.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπερᾶν Μολοσσίαν</span>
			<i>reign through all</i> Molossia, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1248
			</span></i> codd. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pass through, pierce,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνήμην διεπέρασεν Ἀργεῖον δόρυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1394
				</span></i>
			; <i>traverse,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧπαρ,</span> of a vein, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.8
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαπεραίνω</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶσθα διαπερῶν</span>
			<i>by traversing,</i> i.e. <i>by experience,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				994
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. Sch. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>reach, arrive at</i> a place, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFlor.</u>
				247.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> trans., <i>carry over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ ποταμοῦ σῶμα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					151
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				20.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
